{
  "headline": "FDA lists somatropin from Novo Nordisk, Inc. as To Be Discontinued, first posted 2023-01-06; the product at Corvale sites traces to Novo Nordisk plants inspected VAI in 2021 and 2023",
  "headline_cites": ["E15", "D6", "D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows somatropin injection from Novo Nordisk, Inc. with status To Be Discontinued and an initial posting date of 2023-01-06.",
      "cites": ["E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The somatropin 30 mg/3 mL syringes used at Corvale General and Corvale East carry NDC 00169770321 and labeler Novo Nordisk, linking them to the discontinued product.",
      "cites": ["E2", "E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The associated SPL set 1058e17c identifies two registered manufacturing plants: Novo Nordisk A/S - Hax (FEI 3002807748) and Novo Nordisk A/S - Kv (FEI 3015545250).",
      "cites": ["E11", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1167028 at the Kv plant ended 2021-11-18 and was classified VAI, 414 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1238387 at the Hax plant ended 2023-06-01 and was classified VAI, 146 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later inspection 1341150 at the Kv plant ended 2024-05-02, also VAI, 482 days after the posting.",
      "cites": ["D8", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked mitigation is to transfer 3 syringes of the 30 mg/3 mL presentation from Corvale General (14.8 days on hand) to Corvale East (2 days on hand), which would give Corvale East 3 days of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D10"]
    }
  ]
}
